    "['isis enable [parameter1]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set protocols isis interface ge-1/0/0.0', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the translated Juniper equivalent of the HUAWEI command `isis enable 1`:\\n\\n##\\nset protocols isis interface ge-1/0/0.0\\nset protocols isis interface ge-1/0/1.0\\nset protocols isis interface lo0.0\\n##\\n\\nNote: In Juniper:\\n1. Each interface must be explicitly enabled for IS-IS under the protocols hierarchy\\n2. Juniper uses interface naming with unit numbers (e.g., ge-1/0/0.0)\\n3. Loopback interfaces are also explicitly listed\\n4. The \"1\" in HUAWEI\\'s command (which is the IS-IS process ID) isn\\'t needed in Juniper\\'s basic configuration as Juniper doesn\\'t require process IDs for single IS-IS instances', 'trans_template': 'set protocols isis interface ge-1/0/0.0'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set protocols isis interface ge-1/0/1.0', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the translated Juniper equivalent of the HUAWEI command `isis enable 1`:\\n\\n##\\nset protocols isis interface ge-1/0/0.0\\nset protocols isis interface ge-1/0/1.0\\nset protocols isis interface lo0.0\\n##\\n\\nNote: In Juniper:\\n1. Each interface must be explicitly enabled for IS-IS under the protocols hierarchy\\n2. Juniper uses interface naming with unit numbers (e.g., ge-1/0/0.0)\\n3. Loopback interfaces are also explicitly listed\\n4. The \"1\" in HUAWEI\\'s command (which is the IS-IS process ID) isn\\'t needed in Juniper\\'s basic configuration as Juniper doesn\\'t require process IDs for single IS-IS instances', 'trans_template': 'set protocols isis interface ge-1/0/1.0'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set protocols isis interface lo0.0', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the translated Juniper equivalent of the HUAWEI command `isis enable 1`:\\n\\n##\\nset protocols isis interface ge-1/0/0.0\\nset protocols isis interface ge-1/0/1.0\\nset protocols isis interface lo0.0\\n##\\n\\nNote: In Juniper:\\n1. Each interface must be explicitly enabled for IS-IS under the protocols hierarchy\\n2. Juniper uses interface naming with unit numbers (e.g., ge-1/0/0.0)\\n3. Loopback interfaces are also explicitly listed\\n4. The \"1\" in HUAWEI\\'s command (which is the IS-IS process ID) isn\\'t needed in Juniper\\'s basic configuration as Juniper doesn\\'t require process IDs for single IS-IS instances', 'trans_template': 'set protocols isis interface lo0.0'}]]": 1,
    "['isis enable [parameter1]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set protocols isis interface ge-1/0/0.0', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"##\\nset protocols isis interface ge-1/0/0.0\\nset protocols isis interface ge-1/0/1.0\\nset protocols isis interface lo0.0\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n1. In Juniper, ISIS is enabled per interface under the `protocols isis` hierarchy.\\n2. Each physical interface (ge-1/0/0, ge-1/0/1) and loopback (lo0) needs to be explicitly listed.\\n3. Juniper uses .0 as the default unit number for interface references in protocol configurations.\\n4. Unlike Huawei where you specify the ISIS process ID (1), Juniper doesn't require this in basic configurations as it defaults to a single ISIS instance.\", 'trans_template': 'set protocols isis interface ge-1/0/0.0'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set protocols isis interface ge-1/0/1.0', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"##\\nset protocols isis interface ge-1/0/0.0\\nset protocols isis interface ge-1/0/1.0\\nset protocols isis interface lo0.0\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n1. In Juniper, ISIS is enabled per interface under the `protocols isis` hierarchy.\\n2. Each physical interface (ge-1/0/0, ge-1/0/1) and loopback (lo0) needs to be explicitly listed.\\n3. Juniper uses .0 as the default unit number for interface references in protocol configurations.\\n4. Unlike Huawei where you specify the ISIS process ID (1), Juniper doesn't require this in basic configurations as it defaults to a single ISIS instance.\", 'trans_template': 'set protocols isis interface ge-1/0/1.0'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set protocols isis interface lo0.0', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"##\\nset protocols isis interface ge-1/0/0.0\\nset protocols isis interface ge-1/0/1.0\\nset protocols isis interface lo0.0\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n1. In Juniper, ISIS is enabled per interface under the `protocols isis` hierarchy.\\n2. Each physical interface (ge-1/0/0, ge-1/0/1) and loopback (lo0) needs to be explicitly listed.\\n3. Juniper uses .0 as the default unit number for interface references in protocol configurations.\\n4. Unlike Huawei where you specify the ISIS process ID (1), Juniper doesn't require this in basic configurations as it defaults to a single ISIS instance.\", 'trans_template': 'set protocols isis interface lo0.0'}]]": 1
